# The build context. The builder stage copies only package*.json, tsconfig.json
# and src/, so most of this is belt-and-braces — but the context is still
# uploaded to the daemon in full before any COPY runs, and every file in it is a
# file that can bust the cache. Keeping it tight keeps `docker build` fast.
#
# Most important: .env must never enter the context. A secret is readable in an
# intermediate layer forever, even when the runtime stage only copies dist/.

.env
.env.*
*.log

node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.mcp.json

# local experimentation scripts, never part of a build
play/

# operational scripts run with tsx on a developer machine; the compiled
# entrypoints the image needs (server, worker, migrate) are all under src/
scripts/

docs
*.md
*.png

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose-test.yml

# typechecks scripts/ — not part of `npm run build`
tsconfig.scripts.json
